            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Thomas Paine</strong><br>\nThomas Paine was born in Thetford, England, on January 29, 1737. His father was a Quaker and his mother was an Anglican. Paine received a basic education before he started working with his father as a corset maker. He held several jobs, including a privateer, tax officer, and schoolteacher before emigrating to America in 1774, carrying with him ideas of individual liberty and democratic governance.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Paine's Arrival in America</strong><br>\nUpon arriving in America, Paine quickly became involved in the revolutionary cause. With the help of Benjamin Franklin, he secured a job as editor of the Pennsylvania Magazine. His experience in America, combined with his writing skills, would soon catapult him to the center of revolutionary politics and ideology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"Common Sense\" and American Independence</strong><br>\nIn 1776, Thomas Paine wrote \"Common Sense,\" a pamphlet that argued for American independence from Britain. It was written in clear, persuasive prose that was accessible to the general population. The pamphlet sold nearly 500,000 copies, immensely influencing American public opinion and the declaration of the Revolutionary War.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
